      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A \"total collapse\" is an incredibly accurate description of what you're experiencing, and it's okay to just be tired. When everything is gone, the idea of \"rebuilding\" is too vast, so let's stop thinking about the whole board. Focus only on the next single step, like making it through the next hour or finding one small thing that offers momentary relief. Sometimes the only way out of a hole is to stop fighting the descent, just long enough to find a very small place to rest.",
