      "content": "When you feel like the struggle is pointless, it's because your entire sense of self was tied up in the outcome of that fight. If the hole feels bottomless, that's your mind telling you that the *effort* was the only thing that gave you structure. But even if the external structure is gone, you still have your capacity to feel, to observe, and to simply *be*. Don't try to climb out of the hole right now; just focus on finding the most comfortable spot within it for a while.",
